<title>UK: Eagles dives to discount on UK AIM debut.</title>
<headline>Eagles dives to discount on UK AIM debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Eagles Plc, owners of the English rugby league club Sheffield Eagles, dropped on Wednesday to a discount to their issue price on their first day of dealings on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM).</p>
<p>Eagles' shares, issued at 40p, fell 4-1/2p to 35-1/2p by 1320 GMT in thin volume.</p>
<p>&quot;I reckon only one percent of the issue has been turned over today,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>&quot;There is very little demand either way,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The company raised 750,000 stg from the AIM flotation and said it will use the funds for additional working capital.</p>
<p>the British squad, but has found the going tough in the European Super League so far this season with only three wins from 10 games.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
